# Multi-Tenancy and Security

Supports `.project-overview.mdc` and `architecture.mdc`.

## Tenancy

If a resource is tenant-owned, every read/write/search includes tenant context.

- Backend enforces isolation; frontend filtering is not security
- No cross-tenant fetch, join, or RAG retrieval
- Repository methods take `tenantId` (or equivalent) explicitly
- Propagate tenant context from TypeScript to Python on every AI/RAG HTTP call and event
- Python must never retrieve data across tenants; every AI/RAG operation must carry enough tenant context to isolate results

## Authorization

Authentication ≠ authorization. Check permissions server-side, including AI tool execution.

Examples: `conversation.read`, `conversation.assign`, `conversation.escalate`, `ticket.manage`, `knowledge.manage`, `analytics.view`.

## Secrets

Environment variables only. Document names in `.env.example` with empty/placeholder values. Never hardcode API keys, JWT secrets, DB credentials, LLM keys, or webhook secrets. Never commit `.env`.

## Hardening

- Validate all external input (HTTP, WS, webhooks, queues, files, AI output, provider responses)
- Rate-limit sensitive APIs
- Validate webhooks
- Do not log secrets, tokens, or unnecessary PII
- Restrict AI tools; authorize each call
- Protect against prompt injection; model output cannot bypass auth or tenant checks
